    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When dealing with deliberately disruptive behavior, frame the discipline around violations of company policies regarding conduct and professional standards, rather than intent. Document instances where their actions directly violated established rules, such as undermining authority or creating a hostile work environment. If the behavior is intentionally malicious, treating it as gross misconduct may warrant skipping the standard progressive steps for immediate, serious disciplinary action.",
      "source": "target",
